# Title: Potential CommandLine Path Traversal Via Cmd.EXE
# ID: 087790e3-3287-436c-bccf-cbd0184a7db1
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: xknow @xknow_infosec, Tim Shelton
# Date: 2020-06-11
# Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1059.003
# Description: Detects potential path traversal attempt via cmd.exe. Could indicate possible command/argument confusion/hijacking
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((((ParentCommandLine CONTAIN "/c" OR ParentCommandLine CONTAIN "/k" OR ParentCommandLine CONTAIN "/r")) OR ((CommandLine CONTAIN "/c" OR CommandLine CONTAIN "/k" OR CommandLine CONTAIN "/r"))) AND ((ParentImage="*\\cmd.exe") OR (Image="*\\cmd.exe") OR (OriginalFileName = "cmd.exe")) AND ((ParentCommandLine = "/../../") OR (CommandLine CONTAIN "/../../"))) AND NOT ((CommandLine CONTAIN "\\Tasktop\\keycloak\\bin\\/../../jre\\bin\\java")))
